AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming the digital healthcare ecosystem, reshaping how healthcare providers diagnose, treat, and monitor patients. Among the developing AI technologies, generative AI (Gen AI) models, like generative pretrained transformers and generative adversarial networks, demonstrate an exceptional ability to generate synthetic data and process natural language, advancing fields like diagnostics and medical imaging. Although only 35% of healthcare providers currently incorporate AI, about 60% of organizations using Gen AI to report positive return on investment (ROI), underscoring the technology's value potential. This chapter explores the role of AI and Gen AI in healthcare, with applications in drug discovery, personalized medicine, and predictive analytics driving a shift toward smarter, patient-centered care. However, challenges persist, especially regarding ethical considerations and the interpretability of “black-box” AI models. As healthcare advances, quantum computing and 6G networks promise to expand AI capabilities, enabling global, real-time diagnostics and treatment. This chapter offers a comprehensive overview of AI's transformative role in healthcare, while addressing the integration challenges that must be overcome to create a more responsive, efficient, and accessible healthcare landscape.
